    {
      "id": "a2ac527c11b38a6be51efeb7dbdd0686a6f58e2b",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2435257771,
          "type": null,
          "body": "This broke again the auto width adjustment. This time, it is too narrow and doesn't include the space for the related packet info.\n\n![immagine](/uploads/d9736bafc163c61cbb04ec4c91c927b8/immagine.png)\n\nIn the meanwhile I updated Qt from 6.5.3 to 6.8.3, but I don't know if the two things are related.\n\nAnyways, reverting this commit fixes the issue on my side.",
          "author": {
            "id": 18219493,
            "username": "giovanni.musto",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Giovanni Musto",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b8ca1135be5e614246a54ed49c6809a9b172aafdcb27c2db7ec5548b625e76d5?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/giovanni.musto"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-04-04T14:22:54.760Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-04-04T14:22:54.760Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 374297029,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 19463,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "8c4f9c136c543c4272d0509e370b6827f5c645e5",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2435642273,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Ugh, that is annoying, it doesn't like the decoration with no height, but giving it a height of 1 increases the row height by 1 pixel on some platforms (why?). So we could do the size hint twice, once with and once without the decoration, and save the width from one and the height from the other. Amazing.\n\nOr we could live with \"oh no, we've increased the row height by 1 pixel by fixing the other issue.\"",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-04-04T18:38:33.434Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-04-05T08:09:45.475Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 374297029,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 19463,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2436077905,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I would really like to avoid the extra height on every row. Back in the GTK days we put a lot of effort into keeping the height as small as possible.\n\nI seldom use the auto with adjustment feature, so if this has to be kept I'm tempted to make an advanced preference to turn this off.",
          "author": {
            "id": 4753670,
            "username": "stigbjorlykke",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Stig Bjørlykke",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/905aafc6b50e246885f5ea9273a9dc4f22e2658b71f9a1b551b797082bec3f80?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/stigbjorlykke"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-04-05T08:09:45.376Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-04-05T08:09:45.376Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 374297029,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 19463,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2436117764,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I think I've found a somewhat ugly solution: !19473 \n\nIn my opinion this seems like a Qt bug. A decoration positioned to the left of the text should not affect the height if the decoration height (plus any border) is smaller than the sizeHint of the text without the decoration.\n\nYet it always increases the sizeHint height by at least 2.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-04-05T10:35:29.027Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-04-05T10:35:29.027Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 374297029,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 19463,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2436118821,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "It appears to be done intentionally, to \"keep icons from overlapping\":\nhttps://github.com/qt/qtbase/blob/a0e0425a107aebf8727673505ea2376400b54b07/src/widgets/styles/qcommonstyle.cpp#L5027",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-04-05T10:39:42.434Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-04-05T10:39:42.434Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 374297029,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 19463,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2436120917,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "You can see the bug report that led to adding the extra two pixels:\nhttps://bugreports.qt.io/browse/QTBUG-52353\n\nSince we only draw near the border with a straight line that is supposed to connect, we don't need the extra height.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-04-05T10:47:15.679Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-04-05T10:47:15.679Z",
